+Limits are 2 MB of UTF-8 source and 500 total passages. Exhaustive library testing
+stops and fails above 10,000 complete paths rather than silently claiming coverage.
+
+Rejected: variables, Harlowe/SugarCube macros, code/style/startup tags, hooks,
+HTML, link setters, external links, inline links embedded in prose, prose after
+choices, special runtime passages, ambiguous destinations and unrecognized tags.
+Reserved syntax may also reject otherwise literal prose; explicit manual review
+is needed. Do not delete rejected logic merely to make the importer pass.
+
+## Rights are supplied, not inferred
+
+Fill `examples/twee-metadata.template.json` from the actual author's licence or
+public-domain evidence. Default permissions are false and review is unreviewed.
+The command requires source and evidence URLs, original author, attribution,
+applicable territories, notes, reviewer/date, and explicit translation and
+distribution permissions. It does **not** establish whether these assertions are
+true or whether they satisfy all licence terms. Attribution is not permission.
+No licence is assigned to third-party content by this tool.
+
+## Commands
+
+```sh
+# Validate without writing anything.
+node tools/import-twee.mjs --source /path/work.twee --metadata /path/rights.json --check
+
+# Add a new directory and append its exact version to the catalog.
+node tools/import-twee.mjs --source /path/work.twee --metadata /path/rights.json --story-root stories
+
+npm test
+npm run validate:library
+npm run build
+```
+
+Registration uses an exclusive catalog lock shared with the Wikisource importer,
+staged writes and a final atomic catalog replacement. Existing story IDs and
+folders are never overwritten by the Twee command. A failed conversion makes no
+catalog changes. A lock left by an interrupted process requires inspection before
+manual recovery; it is not silently removed by another importer.
+
+Each imported work stores canonical nodes, source text, import metadata, source
+hashes, validation and attribution. `verify-library.mjs` recompiles newly imported
+Twee sources and compares nodes, metadata and manifest exactly. A mismatch fails.
+All files remain server-side; only the current scene is served.
+
+## Test-only sources
+
+`tests/fixtures/static-twee` is synthetic data, clearly marked `test_fixture`.
+Production library loading refuses that marker. These fixtures validate multiple
+work support but are **not** additional published stories. The real catalog still
+contains only *Consider the Consequences!* until an eligible work is imported.
+
+Primary format references:
+- https://github.com/iftechfoundation/twine-specs/blob/master/twee-3-specification.md
+- https://twinery.org/cookbook/terms/terms_passages.html
